# Static IP assignments for devices
# Format: mac_address|ip_address|name
# These are applied as dnsmasq static leases on the router.
# IPs should be outside your DHCP pool or within it (dnsmasq reserves them).
#
# This is optional but useful for:
# - Consistent device identification in logs
# - Port forwarding
# - The parental control works on MAC addresses, so static IPs are not required

aa:bb:cc:00:00:04|192.168.1.10|device_a
aa:bb:cc:00:00:01|192.168.1.11|device_b
AA:BB:CC:00:00:09|192.168.1.20|printer

